Package: bssd
Type: Package
Title: Bayesian Safety Signal Detection for Blinded Clinical Trial Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Gosuke", "Homma", email = "gosuke.homma@astellas.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6854-5627"))
Description: Computes the posterior probability of a safety signal from
    blinded clinical trial data with the models of Duncan (2026)
    <doi:10.1080/10543406.2024.2395532>: the Poisson-based model of
    Mukhopadhyay, Waterhouse and Hartford (2018) <doi:10.1002/pst.1898> with
    the total exposure time or the total time at risk, the exponential
    Bernoulli mixture model, and the log-logistic Bernoulli mixture model.
    All posterior quantities are obtained by numerical integration instead
    of Markov chain Monte Carlo sampling.
